# KNOB GLIDE (Setup's SEL list, the FM-1's setting): with it on and the sequencer playing, a knob turned by hand walks
# its parameter to the new value over N bars, on the sequencer's sixteenths. The project holds the target at once, the
# engine (epar) hears the walk, a step lock still wins on its step, a stop lands the walk. A walk begins on the
# sequencer's second sixteenth (tick 2: "bars 0.125" waits for it, with a sixteenth to spare); a bar is 16 sixteenths
wait 300
projnew
bpm 120
expect glidebars 0
# off (the default) is a knob as ever: the engine has the value at once, nothing walks
knob 2 cut 0
tap PLAY
expect playing 1
glide 2 cut 100
expect par2.cut 100
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 100
expect glides 0
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
# the pick: off at 0, 1 bar, up to 64 with the encoder, no further either way
tap GLO
turn SELECT 5
expect page Setup
tap SEL
row KNOB GLIDE
rowtext off
spin ALGO -1
expect glidebars 0
rowtext off
spin ALGO 1
expect glidebars 1
rowtext 1 bar
spin ALGO 63
expect glidebars 64
rowtext 64 bars
spin ALGO 5
expect glidebars 64
rowtext 64 bars
turn ALGO -200
expect glidebars 0
rowtext off
spin ALGO 4
expect glidebars 4
rowtext 4 bars
wait 100
shot glide_setup.png
tap HOME
# the transport stopped: a knob is immediate even with glide on
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
glide 2 cut 100
expect par2.cut 100
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 100
expect glides 0
# 4 bars from 0 to 64 is a step a sixteenth: the project has the target, the engine is at 0, then 16, 32 and the target
# (1, 2 and 4 bars in), and the walk is over
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
expect tick 2
glide 2 cut 64
expect par2.cut 64
expect glides 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 0
bars 1
wait 20
expect tick 18
expect epar2.cut 16
bars 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 32
expect par2.cut 64
bars 2
wait 20
expect tick 66
expect epar2.cut 64
expect glides 0
# back down, over a span the length does not divide (63 over 64): the nearest value, a half away from the start
tap PLAY
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 1
expect par2.cut 1
bars 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 48
bars 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 32
bars 2
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 1
expect glides 0
# a turn on a walk starts the new walk where the engine is: 2 bars up to 64, back to 0 from there (not from the old
# start, nor from the old target): 32 at the turn, 16 two bars on, 0 at four
tap PLAY
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 64
bars 2
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 32
glide 2 cut 0
expect par2.cut 0
expect glides 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 32
bars 2
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 16
bars 2
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 0
expect glides 0
# a stop lands the walk on its target at once
tap PLAY
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 64
bars 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 16
tap PLAY
expect playing 0
wait 40
expect epar2.cut 64
expect par2.cut 64
expect glides 0
# a step lock wins on its step and lets go after it, the walk is the base under it: T2 plays steps 1 and 3, the lock
# (cut 40) on step 1; on step 1 the lock holds 40 while the base walks on (16, then 18 after step 3)
step 2 1 1 60 100
step 2 1 3 62 100
lock 2 1 1 cut 40
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 64
bars 1
wait 20
expect tick 18
expect live2.cut 40
expect epar2.cut 16
bars 0.125
wait 20
expect live2.cut -1
expect epar2.cut 18
tap PLAY
expect epar2.cut 64
# ... a kit plays its engine copy, which the lock holds at 40 while the walk goes on under it (key 1's cut: 16 by now)
step 1 1 1 36 100
lock 1 1 1 d1.cut 40
knob 1 d1.cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 1 d1.cut 64
bars 1
wait 20
expect par1.d1.cut 64
expect live1.d1.cut 40
expect epar1.d1.cut 40
tap PLAY
# a discrete knob never walks (a filter type, an engine's choice), and a MIDI controller does not either: both at once
knob 2 cut 10
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 ftype 2
glide 2 vmode 1
expect par2.ftype 2
expect glides 0
wait 20
expect epar2.ftype 2
expect epar2.vmode 1
midi B1 4A 41
wait 20
expect par2.cut 65
expect epar2.cut 65
expect glides 0
# the knob itself: ENV's first knob (the attack of T2) walks, the project shows the turn's end (ten clicks, each a new
# walk from where the engine is: still at 0, the last one ends after 4 bars, a sixteenth or two on)
tap EDIT
turn ALGO 1
tap ENV
expect page Envelope
spin K1 10
expect par2.a 10
expect glides 1
wait 20
expect epar2.a 0
bars 5
wait 20
expect epar2.a 10
expect glides 0
tap PLAY
tap HOME
# the ninth walk lands the oldest at its target and takes its place: eight walks (T2..T5, cut and res, from 0 to 100),
# then T6's cut: T2's cut is at 100 now, the others are still at 0, and there are still eight
knob 2 cut 0
knob 2 res 0
knob 3 cut 0
knob 3 res 0
knob 4 cut 0
knob 4 res 0
knob 5 cut 0
knob 5 res 0
knob 6 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 100
glide 2 res 100
glide 3 cut 100
glide 3 res 100
glide 4 cut 100
glide 4 res 100
glide 5 cut 100
glide 5 res 100
expect glides 8
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 0
glide 6 cut 100
expect glides 8
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 100
expect epar2.res 0
expect epar6.cut 0
expect par6.cut 100
bars 4
wait 20
expect epar2.res 100
expect epar5.res 100
expect epar6.cut 100
expect glides 0
tap PLAY
# a track's new engine ends its walks (and only its): T2's and T3's cut under way, T2 changes engine
knob 2 cut 0
knob 3 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 100
glide 3 cut 100
expect glides 2
knob 2 engine 1
expect glides 1
tap PLAY
wait 40
expect glides 0
expect epar3.cut 100
# a new project ends them all
knob 3 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 3 cut 100
expect glides 1
projnew
expect glides 0
wait 40
expect playing 0
expect glidebars 4
# 1 bar: half way at 8 sixteenths, there at 16
tap GLO
turn SELECT 5
tap SEL
row KNOB GLIDE
spin ALGO -3
expect glidebars 1
tap HOME
bpm 120
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 64
bars 0.5
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 32
bars 0.5
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 64
expect glides 0
tap PLAY
# 64 bars (1024 sixteenths: more than a byte holds), at the fastest tempo (220 BPM) to keep the run short: half way at 32 bars, there at 64
tap GLO
turn SELECT 5
tap SEL
row KNOB GLIDE
spin ALGO 63
expect glidebars 64
tap HOME
bpm 220
wait 100
expect tempo 220
knob 2 cut 0
wait 20
tap PLAY
bars 0.125
glide 2 cut 127
bars 32
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 64
bars 31
wait 20
expect glides 1
expect epar2.cut 125
bars 1
wait 20
expect epar2.cut 127
expect glides 0
tap PLAY
# the setting is the FM-1's: a new project keeps it, a saved one comes back with it after a restart
projnew
expect glidebars 64
projsave 1
reboot
wait 400
expect glidebars 64
